<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mask of Sargon</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as copper head from Nineveh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mask of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon</a> is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> alloy head of a ruler found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a>, dating from the Akkadian period. It is often identified with Sargon of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkad">Akkad</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naram-sin">Naram-Sin</a>, though the identification is uncertain. It is a masterpiece of Akkadian metalwork and reflects the empire's lasting artistic legacy.</p></div>
